<article class="env-exercise" id="0298">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0298">Exercise <span data-tag="0298">111.34.6</span>.</a> Consider the schemes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{C}[\{ x_ i\} _{i = 1}^{8}, s, t] /(1 + s x_1^3 + s^2 x_2^3 + t x_3^3 + st x_4^3 + s^2t x_5^3 + t^2 x_6^3 + st^2 x_7^3 + s^2t^2 x_8^3))  \]
</div>
  <p> and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  S = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{C}[s, t])  \]
</div>
  <p> and the morphism of schemes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \pi : X \longrightarrow S  \]
</div>
  <p> Show there does not exist a nonempty open $U \subset S$ and a morphism $\sigma : U \to X$ such that $\pi \circ \sigma = \text{id}_ U$. </p>
</article>